\description{
\code{geom_freqpoly_fade()} draws a frequency polygon (like
\code{\link[ggplot2:geom_histogram]{ggplot2::geom_freqpoly()}}) filled with a linear gradient that fades from
opaque at the top to transparent at the baseline, using
\code{\link[grid:patterns]{grid::linearGradient()}}.
}
\section{Coordinate systems}{

\code{geom_freqpoly_fade()} only supports linear gradients. When used with
\code{\link[ggplot2:coord_radial]{ggplot2::coord_polar()}} or \code{\link[ggplot2:coord_radial]{ggplot2::coord_radial()}}, the geom falls back
to standard area rendering (equivalent to \code{\link[ggplot2:geom_ribbon]{ggplot2::geom_area()}}), which
means no gradient fill is added. The geom emits a warning in this case.
